course: dictionary
lesson: 10322
title: Trader: a person who buys and sells
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A trader is a person who buys and sells goods to make money. A market trader sells fruit, cloth or toys on a stall, and a street trader sells on the street. The clues around the word tell you what kind of trader is meant.
explain: «Britain bought lots of tea from China and paid in silver; British traders then sold opium in China to get silver back.» Here traders are people doing business, buying and selling goods. Try your meaning in the sentence: British people who buy and sell goods fits well.
explain: Some traders travel far from home. «Traders travelled in caravans of camels, resting in oasis towns.» A trader here carries goods over long distances, not just at a local market. Context helps you see that a trader can work in faraway places.
fact: A trader is a person who buys and sells goods to make money.
fact: A market trader sells goods at a market, and a street trader sells goods on the street.
fact: A sole trader is a business run by one person.
fact: In history, traders carried spices, silk and furs between faraway lands.
fact: Traders travelled the Silk Road, and Viking traders sailed to new lands.
exercise: What is a trader? | A farm animal that gives milk | A person who only plays music in a band | *A person who buys and sells goods to make money | A kind of ship that sails the sea
exercise: «Traders carried goods like spices, silk and furs between faraway lands.» What were the traders carrying? | Books and paper | Sand and stones | Bikes and cars | *Spices, silk and furs
exercise: «Traders travelled in caravans of camels.» Which animal did the caravans use? | Elephants | *Camels | Dogs | Horses
test: In «market trader», what does the word market tell you? | The trader's age | *Where the trader sells | The price of the goods | The trader's name
test: «After the conquests, the Mongol lands were peaceful enough for traders to travel safely across Asia.» What does this tell you about traders? | They were always stuck at home | They never left their own village | *They could travel long distances in safety | They only sold tea in one town
exam: A trader buys a bag of rice for £10 and sells it for £15. What is the profit? | *£5 | £10 | £25 | £15
